        <p>NOTlCE.—Solvers who become entitled to &amp;prize in this compltition can, if they desire, have any book on the game of Draughts equal to the value of 53. insteal of cash prize, by notifying the Draughts Editor.</p>
        <p>In connection with the above competition we may state that we offer a mouthlv pr;ze of 5,; to the competitor who succeeds in placing himself at the head of the Solvers' List at the end of the month. Where the prize is awarded the winner's Acore is Cancelled, while the remß.ining competitors' p Ante go towards the next month' 4 competition. The win- ner may re-enter the competition if he chooAes, commencing again at the bottom of the list. Points are awarded as follows: Two for the correct solu- tion of a problem, two for showing a dwll solution, two for correcting the author's terms, and one for each minor correction. Intending competitors may commence at any time.</p>
