        <head>NEWS OF TETE GIME.</head>
        <p>NEWS OF TETE GIME.</p>
        <p>MAZA3L AND A. JORDkN.—Mazant, the auto- maton, is drawing czood audiences, and has measured swords with some of the best talent in London. fie has proved himself a player of the first rank, and among his latest victims was Mr. Alfred Jordan, the champion of London. Of course Jordan ventured upon his favouiite opening, the "Fife." O,At of six games he played this four times, with drawn results. It will be remembered that in the last " International " Jordan secured a neat win on this opening from that clever young player, C. Buchanan, of Glasgow. Mazam,however, surprised Jordan by defeating him in a "Single Corner " game. Jordan, who had the Blacks, con- siders himself almost invincible with the Black side of this opening The following is the game : "SINGLE COTII,TOR."</p>
        <p>11-15 12-16 1-5 3 3 21-25 17-22 22-18 21-7 24-19 24-19 31-24 19-15 15-23 8-12 15-24 17-21 2 7 11— 7 25-18 17-13 28-19 26-22 9 2 4 8 8-11 7-10 14-17 14-17 25-30 22-26 29 27-24 27-24 33 -23 (A) 2-11 8— 3 4 8 9-14 5 9 9-14 (z) 30— 7 7 2 24-20 18— 9 22-18 18— 9(c) 22-13 3 7 10-15 5-14 10-14 11-27 7-11 7-11 25-22 32-27 19-15 23 4 24-19 15— 8 White wins (A) jordan expected 31-23. The text move was evidently net in his book. (n) If 21-25, then 15-10, 6-21, 13-5, 2-9, 22 —8 would leave Black with a doubtful game. (c) Alter this move the play is all forced.</p>
        <p>If any of our readers feel inclined to try conclu- eions with this wonderful machine that plays draughts, now is their opportunity, as it is being exhibited this week in the Free Trade Hall, Man- chester, and plays all corners at 6d a game.</p>
        <p>The small diagnun wit enable our readers t understand the notation by which the moves of the game are recorded. Black c,upies the 3c:ware3 num- bered 1 to 12 and white those numbered 21 to 32. The figures thus (11-15) indicate that a move is made from find to the squares so numbered. Black has the opening move and the pairs of figures apply alternately to 131,ck and White to the close.</p>
