      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1899-10-13_WidnesExaminer_art0033" n="art0033">
        <head>TEMPERLNCR HALL, LATCHFORD.</head>
        <p>TEMPERLNCR HALL, LATCHFORD.</p>
        <p>The usual weekly meeting of the I.otchford Good Templars was held in the Temperants Hall, Latchford, on Monday evening, and was presided over by Bra. Allman (Chief Templar). After the usual business had been tranQacted, the meeting was thrown open, and a concert was held. Shore addresses were delivered by several of the mem- b.qs.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1899-10-13_WidnesExaminer_art0034" n="art0034">
        <head>SPIRITUALISM.</head>
        <p>SPIRITUALISM.</p>
        <p>The speaker on Sunday at the Spiritualist Hall, Bewsey-street was Mr. E. Markley. In the after- noon he dealt with a suggested subject? "In the infinite changes of mind and •natter, what is the goal ?” In the evening the subject was "Spiritual- ism and present-day problems," in which he spoke upon the questions of life after c'eath, capital and labour, abundance and poverty, war, the position of woman, &amp;e, and argued that Spiritualism had something to say on all these problems. On Monday evening Mr. Marklew delivered a lecture on "Is In- gersoll in hell ?" THE LITERARY AND PHILOSOPHICAL SOCIETY. The arrangements for the ensuing session are now complete. The pr2sident is the Rev. Morley Stevenson; the vice-president, Mr. J. Rymer Young; the hon. treasurer, Mr William Silcock ; and the hon. secretaries, Messrs J A Edelsten and G Carru- thers. The sessiod will be opened on October 30th by a conversazione at the Training College, by the invitation of the President, and papers will be given during the season by Miss E L Broadbent, the Ven. Archdeacon Wilson. Mr Alfred Darbvshire, the Rev Henry 6.,w (of Leicester), and the Rev F E Powell Altogether about sir or seven meetings will be held.</p>
      </div>
