        <p>No. I.—Mr. Owen, Ty Main Farm, Newberough, writes as follows :—" I can give the highest praise to the valuable remedy, Gwilym Evans' Q iinine Bitters. I had long suffered from DAility and Weakeess,and really thought I should never recover. My medical men were privately of the same opinion. But when I commenced taking this Preeions Medicine,to my ereut surprise and joy, as well as that of my family, I rapidly improved, and now feel myself vite another 13oing ; and I shall ever praise Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters as The Best Remedy for Debility and Weakness. No. 2.—Mr. Edwards, of Williamstown. writes as fol- lows :—" I can safely say that Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters have done wonders for me. Alter suffering for twelve months from Debility, and trying several doctors and different remedies without any benefit, I was ad- vised to try Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters, and the re- sult has been good." No. 3.—r. Brookes. 89. Kelshaw-street, Liverpool, writes as follows :—" I have suffered from Indieestion and Liver Complaint for many years, but alter taking the Wonderful Medicine, Gwilyin Evans' Quinine Bitters for only two months,' am happy to say it has given me great relief." No. 4.—Mr. Evans, 41, Henry-street, Birmingham, writes as follows :—"I have very great pleasure in bear- ing testimony to the benefit I have received from taking Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters. lam never without a boate in the house,and it is invaluable to me. I suffered very much from Indigeslon. Nervousness, and Debility, and often I had very severe pains in my head, soithat to me it has proved quite a boon, as I can rely uifon it to give me relief. I confidently recommeed it to everyone I meet who suffers in the same way, and my recomoten- dation has always proved a blessing," No. s.—Mrs. Kirkham, 31, Dunstall-street, Wolver- hampton, writes as follows :—" I have suffered from Ind'gestion and pains in the Head from three to four ' years, but after taking two bottles of Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters, I feel completely cured, and never felt better in my life." No. 6.—Mrs. Williams, 11, Surrey-lane, Battersea. writes as follows :—" I shall not fail to recommend Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters to all sufferers that come under my notice, as it is a Medicine that I have proved to be more excellent even than what you profess it to be. The World-renowned Preparation is sold in bottles 23 9i and 43 61 each, everywhere,or the Proprietors will forward direct on receipt of stamps to the above value carriage free. The Sole Proprietors are the Quinine Bitters Manufacturing Company, Limited, Llanelly, South Wales. Beware of Imitations. This is most im- portant. When purchasing, always see the name, " Gvvilym Evans " on Label, Stamp, and Bottle,witbout which none are genuine.</p>
